From: baseband lane
Subject: 0531 pandora_pas: read the image back out of the carveout before TrustZone sees it

HakiOS's step_image() writes the modem's segments and then reads every one of them back
("read them back ... %llu words or bytes differ"), and only hands the image to TrustZone when
nothing differs.  This loader wrote them and went straight on to MEM_SETUP and AUTH_AND_RESET.

The cost of not checking is specific to this stage: a carveout mapping that silently refused the
writes would reach TrustZone as a corrupt image, and TrustZone's answer would look like an id or a
permission problem -- which is what this stage has been chasing.  A read-back turns that into

  PANDORA PAS: modem.mdt: read back 70254592 bytes, 0 differ

and, when something is wrong, into an EIO that stops the load before the call, with the difference
count in the log.

The comparison needs each segment's bytes a second time, so one buffer sized to the largest segment
is allocated for the pass (about 11 MiB on this phone) and freed afterwards.  If it cannot be
allocated the message says the image is unverified rather than pretending it passed.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
index 2d045a8..477ba70 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
@@ -379,6 +379,54 @@ pandora_pas_load(const char *prefix, const char *base, unsigned pas, uint64_t me
 		total += ph[i].p_filesz;
 	}
 	__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+	/*
+	 * Read every segment back, as HakiOS's step_image() does ("read them back ... %llu words or
+	 * bytes differ" before it hands the image to TrustZone).  A carveout mapping that silently
+	 * refused the writes would otherwise reach MEM_SETUP and AUTH_AND_RESET as a corrupt image:
+	 * TrustZone would answer with a rejection that looks like an id or a permission problem,
+	 * which is exactly the kind of false lead this stage has already cost days to.
+	 *
+	 * The comparison needs the segment's bytes a second time, so one buffer of the largest
+	 * segment is allocated for the pass; the phone's own largest segment is about 11 MiB.
+	 */
+	if (!err) {
+		uint64_t differ = 0, checked = 0, biggest = 0;
+		vm_offset_t tmp = 0;
+		for (unsigned i = 0; i < phnum; i++) {
+			if (mdt_loadable(&ph[i]) && ph[i].p_filesz > biggest) {
+				biggest = ph[i].p_filesz;
+			}
+		}
+		if (biggest && kmem_alloc(kernel_map, &tmp, (vm_size_t)biggest, KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO,
+		    VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) == KERN_SUCCESS) {
+			for (unsigned i = 0; i < phnum && !err; i++) {
+				if (!mdt_loadable(&ph[i]) || ph[i].p_filesz == 0) {
+					continue;
+				}
+				uint64_t off = (uint64_t)ph[i].p_paddr - reloc_base;
+				if (mdt_segment(prefix, base, mdt, &ph[i], i, (void *)tmp)) {
+					err = EIO;
+					break;
+				}
+				const uint8_t *at = (const uint8_t *)(mem + off);
+				const uint8_t *was = (const uint8_t *)tmp;
+				for (uint32_t k = 0; k < ph[i].p_filesz; k++) {
+					if (at[k] != was[k]) {
+						differ++;
+					}
+				}
+				checked += ph[i].p_filesz;
+			}
+			kmem_free(kernel_map, tmp, (vm_size_t)biggest);
+			printf("PANDORA PAS: %s: read back %llu bytes, %llu differ%s\n", name,
+			    checked, differ, differ ? " -- the image is NOT in place" : "");
+			if (differ) {
+				err = EIO;
+			}
+		} else {
+			printf("PANDORA PAS: %s: no buffer for the read-back, the image is unverified\n", name);
+		}
+	}
 	/*
 	 * The carveout mapping stays.
 	 *
